<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="recommended-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/spell_deathknight_bloodpresence.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Recommended Gear for Blood Death Knight in Mists of Pandaria Classic</span></h2>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="what-is-the-bis-blood-death-knight-gear">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/spell_deathknight_butcher2.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> What is the BiS Blood Death Knight gear?</h3>The <span class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_deathknight.gif");'></span>
<span class="c6">Blood Death Knight's</span> quest for BIS is ever complicated by the fact that we need different gear depending on what the raid needs. In the pre-vengeance era of World of Warcraft, the role of the tank was threefold: Hold threat, reduce the chance of dying as much as possible, and position the boss and adds properly. Mists of Pandaria has supercharged the idea that your Tank is also a member of your DPS roster. <br/>
<br/>Everything from talents to gear to enchants belong on a spectrum between full-beef mode and full-DPS mode, and where you fall on that spectrum will change depending on how comfortable you are with the class, what type of content you're aiming to do, and how much trust you have in the rest of your raid. <b>
<i>It's unlikely that being toward either side of that spectrum will be the best thing for you and your raid group</i></b>, so make gearing adjustments that fit within the context of how you approach the game. <br/>
<br/>You have stat priorities ranging from most defensive to most offensive, and it is recommended that you familiarize yourself with the Blood Death Knight's <a data-contiguous="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/guide/classes/death-knight/blood/tank-stat-priority-pve">stat priorities</a> before considering your best-in-slot loot. Generally, we'll prefer gear that favors <b>Parry</b> and <b>Dodge</b>, but different encounters will call for different gear. While raid drops are generally the most reliable way of getting high-item-level gear, many other items can be just as good, if not better.<ul class="exclude-units"></ul>
<br/>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="bis-gear">Overall Best-in-Slot Gear for Blood Death Knights</h3>Raids releases in Mists of Pandaria Classic will be staggered, with a few resets between each raid opening. This means that as the phase progresses, more of your best-in-slot gear will become available to you. This also means that you will need to find alternatives until your best-in-slot items are available. Below, we have included three gear planners, each corresponding with one of the raid releases.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
